# Left out: what to return when no number repeats. This is the worked
# example from ROADMAP.md §3.6: nobody says "return False", so GAP003 stays.

step 1
add root: for num~loopvar in nums:
    ...
expect gaps GAP002

step 2
fill h1:
    if num in seen:
        return True
expect gaps GAP001 GAP003

step 3
add root start: seen = set()
expect gaps GAP003

step 4
set n7.orelse = seen.add(num)  # ~synonym
expect gaps GAP003
or
add n2: seen.add(num)  # ~synonym
expect gaps GAP003
